  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up a socialised model of domestic waste and plastics management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the success of earlier UNDP project &quot;Socialised Domestic Waste Management Programme&quot; implemented by the city of Hoi An in 2010-2012, this project replicates and expands this approach in other cities of Vietnam. Specifically, this project will target and scale up the model of waste management across five sites: Ha Long Bay, Quy Nhon Bay, Binh Thuan (Mui Ne) , Binh Duong, and Da Lat over the 2.5 years (2019-2021).</narrative>
  </description>
